          "text": "{\"schema_version\":\"ai-evaluator-v2/1.1\",\"case_id\":\"3-4\",\"candidate_id\":\"candidate_1\",\"action_assessment\":{\"status\":\"defect\",\"summary\":\"The graph correctly includes sending the questionnaire and sending reminders, but it incorrectly repeats the questionnaire-sending action after each reminder, which is unsupported by the source.\"},\"flow_assessment\":{\"status\":\"preserved\",\"summary\":\"The required precedence that the questionnaire is sent before reminders is preserved, and reminders remain recurrently reachable; the extra questionnaire resend does not by itself break matched-action precedence.\"},\"control_flow_assessment\":{\"status\":\"defect\",\"summary\":\"The retry loop is modeled incorrectly: after a no-response outcome, the process sends a reminder and then loops back to sending the questionnaire again, instead of continuing the reminder cycle until the completed questionnaire is received.\"},\"main_error_type\":\"wrong_loop_or_recurrence\",\"explanation\":\"The source describes one initial questionnaire followed, if needed, by repeated reminders every five days until the completed questionnaire is received. The generated graph captures the initial questionnaire, a success/continue decision, and recurring reminders, but its retry path goes from reminder back to 'send questionnaire to claimant.' That changes the recurrence behavior from repeated reminders to reminder-plus-questionnaire resend cycles. This is a material semantic change, though the overall claim-handling pattern is still partly preserved.\",\"overall_score\":0.68,\"severity\":\"moderate\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"ambiguity_flag\":false,\"ambiguity_explanation\":\"\",\"requires_human_review\":false,\"review_reason\":\"\"}"
